# Architecture Rules

You are building NOIR Commerce OS, a premium fashion ecommerce platform.

Do not build random pages. Build a scalable product architecture.

## Core Architecture

Use feature-based architecture.

Preferred structure:

src/
  app/
  components/
    ui/
    layout/
    commerce/
    motion/
  features/
    auth/
    products/
    cart/
    checkout/
    wishlist/
    account/
    admin/
    orders/
    search/
    reviews/
  hooks/
  lib/
  services/
  store/
  types/
  utils/
  styles/

## Rules

- Keep business logic inside `features/`.
- Keep reusable UI inside `components/ui/`.
- Keep layout components inside `components/layout/`.
- Keep API/Supabase logic inside `services/` or `lib/`.
- Keep Zustand stores inside `store/`.
- Keep shared TypeScript types inside `types/`.
- Keep helper functions inside `utils/`.

## Non-Negotiables

- No duplicated components.
- No duplicated business logic.
- No massive files.
- No hardcoded repeated data.
- No random folder creation.
- No mixing UI, API, and business logic in one file.
- No placeholder architecture.

## Component Rules

Every reusable component must support:

- loading state
- error state
- empty state when relevant
- disabled state
- focus state
- hover state
- responsive behavior
- accessibility
- dark theme
- clean props

## Naming Rules

Use PascalCase for components.

Example:

ProductCard.tsx
CartDrawer.tsx
CheckoutStepper.tsx

Use camelCase for utilities.

Example:

formatCurrency.ts
calculateSubtotal.ts
validateCoupon.ts

Use kebab-case only for route paths.

## Import Rules

Prefer absolute imports when configured.

Example:

import { Button } from "@/components/ui/Button"

Avoid deep messy imports.

## Page Rules

Every page must include:

- clear purpose
- premium layout
- responsive design
- loading state
- error state
- empty state where relevant
- SEO metadata when applicable
- no dead buttons
- no blank sections

## Data Rules

Do not hardcode production data directly inside components.

Use:

- data files for demo content
- services for backend data
- hooks for fetching
- stores for client state

## Scalability Rules

Build as if the project will support:

- thousands of products
- thousands of users
- admin dashboard
- payments
- inventory
- orders
- analytics
- future mobile app

## Quality Rule

A feature is not complete when it works.

A feature is complete when it is:

- reusable
- accessible
- responsive
- performant
- secure
- maintainable
- visually premium